// os::exit ends the run with its code, a negative one too, after nothing else: the buffered
// line is never written. `ctxc interp` and `ctxc run` end the same way; the code is -3 as
// Windows reports it, and its low byte, 253, elsewhere.
//# $ ctxc interp {dir}/exit.ctx --
//# [windows] exit: -3
//# [posix] exit: 253
//# $ ctxc run {dir}/exit.ctx --
//# [windows] exit: -3
//# [posix] exit: 253
